# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# RiseUp Mobile — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY
#
# This file configures a development build, and nothing else. Its JS is
# bundled by Metro on this machine, so these are the values that end up in it.
#
# PREVIEW AND PRODUCTION DO NOT READ THIS FILE. They bundle in the cloud, and
# their values live on EAS, which is the single source of truth for them:
#
#   npx eas-cli env:list --environment production
#   npx eas-cli env:set --name X --value Y --environment production --visibility plaintext
#
# `eas.json` deliberately has no `env` blocks. A value there silently overrides
# the remote variable of the same name, which is how two people end up reading
# different values for one setting.
#
# Metro INLINES these at build time, so after any change restart with
# `npx expo start --clear`. A fast refresh will not pick them up.
#
# Nothing secret belongs here. A Clerk publishable key and an API host are both
# public by design — they ship inside the app bundle either way — and anything
# that is not public has no business on a device (PRD §11).
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# YOUR machine's LAN address — not localhost, which a phone resolves to itself,
# and not a 172.x WSL or Hyper-V adapter, which a phone cannot route to.
# `ipconfig` will tell you which one is real.
#
# The API must also be bound to 0.0.0.0, or it is reachable only from the
# machine it runs on:  uvicorn api.main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.42:8000

# The DEVELOPMENT Clerk instance, because that is what the local backend
# verifies against (riseup-backend/.env: CLERK_JWKS_URL). The app's key and the
# backend's JWKS must name the same instance or every request fails signature
# verification.
EXPO_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_cHJvbXB0LW1vb3NlLTc0LmNsZXJrLmFjY291bnRzLmRldiQ
